+# Filtered Veterinarian Reads Bypass the Vets Cache
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The veterinarian directory is narrowed by a `specialty` value taken from the request address. Both published forms of the directory accept it.
+
+`VetRepository`'s read methods are annotated `@Cacheable("vets")`. Spring's default key generator builds the key from the method arguments alone, so a filter argument becomes part of the key.
+
+`CacheConfiguration` declares the `vets` cache through the JCache API with statistics enabled and nothing else. Its source comment records that a size limit must come from the provider's own configuration, and none is set. The application has no authentication, so any caller reaches the directory.
+
+The paged read already keys on a caller-supplied page number, so the key space is not caller-free today. A free-text specialty widens it from integers to arbitrary strings.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Cache the filtered read under `vets`.** Rejected: an unauthenticated caller would mint an unbounded number of entries from arbitrary text, in a cache with no size limit and no eviction.
+2. **Cache it under a second, size-limited cache.** Rejected: it buys provider-specific size configuration and a second cache to reason about, for a query the seeded three specialties answer in one indexed join.
+3. **Leave the filtered read uncached** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+The reads that take no specialty stay cached under `vets` and behave exactly as before. The reads that take a caller-supplied specialty are not cached and reach the database on every request. Free-text keys never enter the cache.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A narrowed directory costs one query per request. The clinic's directory is small and the query is a join over two lookup tables, so the cost is bounded.
+- An unnarrowed directory is untouched, which is what the requirement asks for.
+- The two paths can disagree: the cached unnarrowed read may be stale while the narrowed read is fresh. The application has no write path for veterinarians, so this is reachable only through an out-of-band data change — the same gap [Open Question 5](../system-design.md#open-questions-from-the-survey) records.
+- Growth of the cache from caller-supplied page numbers is unchanged. This decision neither widens nor repairs it.
+- Keeping the filtered methods uncached also keeps them clear of the key collision the shared cache name invites, since the default key generator ignores the method name.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003, REQ-VET-004
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the repository and controller rows realizing this decision.
+- [Feature-Package Organization Without a Service Layer](2026-07-31-feature-package-organization.md) — why the query rule lives in the repository rather than a service.
